  "title": "# Build: three-layouts-per-screen (FABLE, high thinking: plugin contract + scaffold = foundation) *…",
  "asked": "# Build: three-layouts-per-screen (FABLE, high thinking: plugin contract + scaffold = foundation) **Name:** Three layouts per screen · **Category:** Framework ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"From now on, all plugin screens get three layouts, and come with a toolbar to select which one, with the toolbar hidden by default.\" Then: \"Not old ones, only new ones.\" Book to a free named agent. **NEW plugins only. Do NOT retrofit existing plugins.** ## Do 1. **Contract**: extend `plugin@1` so each screen a plugin declares can list **3 layout variants** (layout assets or screen-level layout presets: e.g. Compact / Standard / Spacious, or List / Grid / Split, whatever fits the screen) with one marked default. Schema + validator + PORTING.md note. 2. **Layout switcher toolbar**: a shared toolbar asset (`toolbar@1` instance) that switches between a screen's layouts. **Hidden by default**, revealed via right-click on the screen title ('Show layout toolbar'), a setting, or voice. The choice is remembered per screen per device. It's a normal toolbar, so it can be moved/docked/right-click settings like other toolbars. 3. **Scaffold**: `axf new-module`/plugin templates and Build Pilot's plugin wizard generate the 3 layouts + hidden toolbar automatically for every new plugin screen. 4. **Enforce for new plugins only**: a CI check fails if a NEW plugin screen (added after this lands) declares fewer than 3 layouts. Existing plugins are grandfathered via a baseline list. 5. Ties in with UI Review: the review item's Layout dropdown lists the screen's 3 layouts first. 6. Rule in RULES.md / CLAUDE.md / build-brief templates. Basic Markdown readme. Tests, PR **through the merge queue only** (auto-land is OFF). Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM (Brett, voice, Nov 4): UI Review layout choices \"So UI Review will only allow you to select from the three layouts it is going to generate.\" - In each UI Review item, the **Layout dropdown lists ONLY that screen's 3 generated layouts** (from three-layouts-per-screen), with the default marked. No other layout assets. Apply (ui-review-alarm addendum 5) picks which of the 3 becomes the default. - Screens without 3 layouts (old, grandfathered plugins) show the dropdown disabled with \"no layout variants\". Color/Style dropdowns stay preview-only over all installed themes. ## ADDENDUM 2 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) Amber: \"If they all point to the same shared toolbar, change it once and every plugin's view toolbar updates; if you ever want one plugin different, give it its own copy.\" Brett: \"Yep.\" - Every new plugin's layout switcher **references ONE shared toolbar asset** (`axf.toolbar.layout-switcher`), not a copy. Editing that asset (Toolbar designer / right-click settings) changes it in every plugin at once. - Right-click on a plugin's layout toolbar > **'Give this plugin its own copy'** forks it into a plugin-local asset (inherits until edited, using the inherit@1 pattern), and **'Go back to the shared toolbar'** reverts it. Settings show which plugins use the shared one vs a copy. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade